cells=[
["OI-186: the demotion's rewind-beat walk in RTL: its form, for OA to rule (OA 435 (5b), (7))"],
["—"],
["The model builds every rewind beat in the demote's cycle: each lane's oldest unretired uop across the ROB and then the decode queue, lanes at one PC merged into one beat. The doc says the walk is a slow path during the drain. The exact form needs a parallel pick over the ROB and the decode queue in one module. OI proposes a streaming walk, one entry a cycle, sending a beat for each entry that covers new lanes without merging beats at one PC. FET ends with the same PC in every lane. The epoch-only notice and the landed level do not wait on this, and OI builds them now. Needs: OA"],
["What the model does (Core::control, demote): at the demote, take(pc, group_mask) over every valid ROB entry from the head, then over the warp's decode-queue uops; a lane is covered by the first entry holding it; a new beat unless one already has that PC. The epoch-only notice and all beats queue in that cycle and leave one a cycle (A-6). The decode queue's uops of the warp are flushed in the same cycle (OI-58).",
 "Why not the exact form in RTL. The merge by PC needs, for each beat, the oldest entry with uncovered lanes and every other entry at its PC: a rotating prefix OR over 32 group masks, a priority pick, a 31-bit compare against all 32 pc_lo and an OR of their masks, about 35 NGD in one cycle, or two cycles a beat with the first-cover masks registered (1,024 flops a slot). The decode queue's uops sit in another module (ooe_decq), so a merge across both sources crosses modules, and its flush in the squash's cycle would have to wait for the walk.",
 "Proposed form (C), a streaming walk:",
 "(1) ooe_rob_w (slice 6) walks its ROB from the head, one entry a cycle, through one read of the pc_lo and group-mask arrays it already holds, with a 32-bit covered register. An entry with new lanes m sends a beat (pc, m). Then it walks the warp's decode-queue uops, which ooe_decq presents one a cycle on a walk port, in queue order, before it flushes them.",
 "(2) Beats are not merged by PC. Two beats at one PC can happen only when two groups that a squashed branch had split both have uops in flight at the same PC. FET writes each beat's PC into its lanes, so the lane-PC vector is the same and the groups reconverge exactly as with one beat. AR's contract would read 'at most one beat per entry with new lanes' in place of 'one per PC'.",
 "(3) The walk sends at most one beat a cycle, behind the epoch-only notice in ooe_redir's order, and stalls while the channel is busy. landed rises after the last beat lands, as the model's notice_lands does.",
 "(4) Cost: a 32-bit covered register, a walk pointer and a beat payload register a slot. There is no new array, since IS-4's pc and group mask are what it reads. The read mux is the head read's size.",
 "Timing against the model: the walk adds up to (ROB entries + decode-queue uops) cycles before drained. The drain already waits for every memop, so this is off S1's path. OI adds model knobs demote_walk (one entry a cycle) and beat_merge 0, with a control that a lane's PC differs, and RH prices them if OA wants a figure. The bench compares the lane-PC vector at landing, and the beats one for one against the model under the knobs.",
 "Rejected forms: the exact merge (above); a beat table merging by PC, 32 × (47 + 32) flops a slot; and a lane-PC vector, 32 × 47 flops a slot.",
 "Asks of OA: (a) the form, C or exact; (b) under C, whether the decode-queue walk port in ooe_decq, with its flush held until the walk passes, is the right split, or whether the ROB-side walk should read the decode queue another way; (c) whether the model's default takes beat_merge 0 and demote_walk, so that both hosts match the RTL. OI builds the epoch-only notice, the landed timer and the kill path's notice in ooe_redir now; they do not depend on this."]]
